meta {
  name: Invitation imports - Upload
  type: http
  seq: 213
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/invitation-imports
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(path/to/invitations.csv)
  default_role: member
  ~access_groups[]: <cuid of an access group>
  ~member_tags[]: <cuid of a member tag>
}

docs {
  Uploads a CSV file of invitations (#1390, multipart/form-data): UTF-8, a header row with a column email, and the optional columns role, access_groups and tags (names separated by |). At most 1000 rows and 1 MB. The server reads the file one time and does not keep it. 201 with the import in preview: the counts, the ignored columns, and the defaults (default_role, access_groups, member_tags) that every row gets. A new upload deletes the older preview of the caller in this community. An error of the file is a 400 on file. Owner, admins, moderators with manage_members. Token ability: invitations:write. Limited to 5 a minute.
}
